---
// About holds the person; Projects and Websites hold the work. Hero over the levee in pixels,
// the AVE-26 datasheet (pins and photos in src/data/about.json), the longer version, the
// recommendations as pull quotes, why underwater, and a closing band. Its "Garden" palette is in
// src/styles/about.css, scoped by data-page="about".
import '@/styles/about.css';
import '@/styles/hand.css';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/Icon.astro';
import PixelScene from '@/components/about/PixelScene.astro';
import FeatureCard from '@/components/about/FeatureCard.astro';
import Datasheet from '@/components/about/Datasheet.astro';
import Polaroid from '@/components/about/Polaroid.astro';
import PullQuotes from '@/components/about/PullQuotes.astro';
import site from '@/data/site.json';
import gradHall from '@/assets/about/grad-taylor-hall.jpg';
import gradTiger from '@/assets/about/grad-tiger.jpg';
import tigerStadium from '@/assets/about/polaroid-tiger-stadium.jpg';
import familyAdam from '@/assets/about/family-adam.jpg';
import bayouBoat from '@/assets/about/polaroid-bayou-boat.jpg';
import trout from '@/assets/about/polaroid-trout.jpg';
import rampageBuild from '@/assets/about/polaroid-rampage-build.jpg';
import type { ImageMetadata } from 'astro';

// Lafitte after Hurricane Ida: the fourth print in Why underwater, shown once the file is in
// src/assets/about/. TODO(ave): add polaroid-ida.jpg, and the photo credit.
const ida = Object.values(import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>('/src/assets/about/polaroid-ida.{jpg,jpeg,png,webp}', { eager: true }))[0]?.default;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  page="about"
  footer="links"
  description="About Avery Matherne: graduate researcher at LSU, web designer, nonprofit co-founder, and someone who would rather be outside."
>
  <section class="ab-hero g-dark">
    <PixelScene />
    <div class="ab-hero__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap ab-hero__grid">
      <div class="ab-hero__text">
        <h1 class="ab-hero__title">Hi, I'm Ave.</h1>
        <p class="ab-hero__lede">
          Yes, I spend a lot of my day at a screen. Signals by day, websites by night. The rest of the time I'm on a bike on the levee, on a
          mountain, or in a thrift store, usually with a latte.
        </p>
        <div class="ab-btns">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#datasheet">Read my datasheet</a>
          <a class="btn" href={site.resumePdf} download><Icon name="download" /> Résumé (PDF)</a>
        </div>
        <p class="ab-hero__cap">the scene behind this is the levee at dusk, drawn on a 48 by 16 LED grid</p>
      </div>
      <FeatureCard />
    </div>
  </section>

  <Datasheet />

  <section class="wrap ab-long" aria-labelledby="long-title">
    <div class="ab-long__text">
      <h2 id="long-title" class="ab-h2">The longer version</h2>
      {/* TODO(ave): check the sentence about growing up around Adam's doctors, nurses and equipment. */}
      <p>
        I grew up sure I would be a doctor. After my little brother's accident, I grew up around his doctors, nurses and equipment, and I even
        learned to change his trach. I started at LSU on the pre-med track, found out I loved math, and realized what I
        liked about medicine was the systems behind a diagnosis. I wanted to build the solution instead of prescribing it, so I switched to
        computer engineering. I finished the B.S. in May 2026 and stayed for an M.S. in electrical and computer engineering, focused on
        communications and signal processing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since 2020 I've also done title research as a land agent, which mostly means reading old courthouse records until they agree with each
        other. It turns out that's decent training for signal processing. The answer is usually in the part nobody wanted to read.
      </p>
      <div class="ab-long__rp">
        <p>
          The work that hooked me was <a class="link" href="/work/rampage/">RAMpage</a>, a combat robot where I wrote the code that fired the plow,
          and a <a class="link" href="/work/v2v-bsm-ofdm/">radio link</a> I built on two software-defined radios for my communications design course.
          That radio project is why Dr. Aldo Duarte recommended me for the <a class="link" href="/work/onr-intelligent-data-management/">Office of Naval Research project</a> I work on now.
        </p>
        <Polaroid
          photo={rampageBuild}
          alt="Four RAMpage teammates bent over the robot's open chassis at a kitchen counter."
          caption="Build night, 2025"
          tilt={2}
          sizes="(min-width: 720px) 11rem, 55vw"
          class="ab-long__print"
        />
      </div>
      <p>
        Websites happened on the side. I built one for our family's nonprofit, then for a few small businesses, and now I keep four of them
        running.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="ab-grad">
      <Polaroid
        photo={tigerStadium}
        alt="Avery smiling in a white dress in front of Tiger Stadium."
        caption="Tiger Stadium"
        tilt={1.5}
        sizes="(min-width: 960px) 15rem, 60vw"
        class="ab-grad__lead"
      />
      <div class="ab-grad__pair">
        <Polaroid
          photo={gradHall}
          alt="Avery in an LSU graduation gown tossing a cap into the air in front of Patrick F. Taylor Hall."
          caption="Taylor Hall"
          tilt={-2.5}
          sizes="(min-width: 960px) 13rem, 45vw"
        />
        <Polaroid
          photo={gradTiger}
          alt="Avery in a graduation gown hugging the bronze tiger statue on campus."
          caption="the tiger"
          tilt={2}
          sizes="(min-width: 960px) 13rem, 45vw"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="ab-grad__cap">May 2026. One degree down, one to go.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <PullQuotes />

  <section class="ab-why g-dark" aria-labelledby="why-title">
    <div class="wrap ab-why__grid">
      <div class="ab-why__text">
        <p class="ab-why__kicker">Why underwater</p>
        <h2 id="why-title" class="ab-h2 ab-h2--lg">It started with my little brother.</h2>
        <p>
          Adam drowned in our backyard pool at 14 months old, with a house full of family. He survived. In 2020 my siblings and I started Because
          of ADAM to share everything we wish we'd known.
        </p>
        <p>
          Water runs in the family. Both of my grandfathers worked the water in Lafitte, Louisiana, as fishermen and crabbers. When Hurricane Ida
          flooded Lafitte in 2021, my grandpa waded through his own backyard to check on his boats and crab traps. Now I study how sound travels
          through water.
        </p>
        <p>
          A pool alarm listens for a splash. A child in trouble barely makes one. I want to know if a hydrophone can hear the difference, so that's
          what I'm working on, on my own time.
        </p>
        <div class="ab-btns">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/work/acoustic-pool-alarm/">The pool alarm project</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://becauseofadam.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">becauseofadam.org<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-why__prints">
        <Polaroid
          photo={familyAdam}
          alt="Avery and her dad crouched beside her little brother Adam, who is wearing an LSU Tigers jersey and blue sunglasses, on a patio."
          caption="Me, Dad and Adam"
          tilt={-2}
          sizes="(min-width: 960px) 15rem, 45vw"
        />
        <Polaroid
          photo={bayouBoat}
          alt="Avery and her sister Grace in orange life jackets, smiling from the front of a boat on the bayou in Lafitte."
          caption="Lafitte, with Grace"
          tilt={2.5}
          sizes="(min-width: 960px) 15rem, 45vw"
        />
        {
          ida && (
            <Polaroid
              photo={ida}
              alt="Avery's grandpa wading waist-deep across his flooded backyard toward his boat docks on the bayou after Hurricane Ida."
              caption="Lafitte, after Hurricane Ida, 2021"
              tilt={1.5}
              sizes="(min-width: 960px) 15rem, 45vw"
            />
          )
        }
        <Polaroid
          photo={trout}
          alt="Avery in sunglasses kissing a fish she just caught, on a boat near the Gulf."
          caption="June 2026"
          tilt={-1.5}
          sizes="(min-width: 960px) 15rem, 45vw"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="ab-end g-dark" aria-labelledby="end-title">
    <div class="wrap ab-end__row">
      <div>
        <h2 id="end-title" class="ab-h2 ab-h2--lg">Say hi.</h2>
        <p class="ab-end__line">Research, a website, or a thrift store recommendation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-btns">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Send a note</a>
        <a class="btn" href={site.resumePdf} download><Icon name="download" /> Résumé (PDF)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .g-dark {
    background: var(--g-hero);
  }

  .ab-btns {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .ab-h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.6vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .ab-h2--lg {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4.4vw, 3rem);
  }

  /* Hero: two columns, bottom-aligned, over the pixel scene. */
  /* At least as tall as the scene, so all 16 rows show. */
  .ab-hero {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    min-height: calc(100vw / 3);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ab-hero__shade {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(20 42 36 / 0.94) 0%, rgb(20 42 36 / 0.8) 40%, rgb(20 42 36 / 0) 70%);
  }

  .ab-hero__grid {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    padding-block: 3.5rem 4rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .ab-hero__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
      gap: 3.5rem;
      align-items: end;
      padding-block: 3.5rem 4rem;
    }
  }

  /* Stacked, the text sits over the whole scene, so the shade runs top to bottom instead. */
  @media (max-width: 959px) {
    .ab-hero__shade {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgb(20 42 36 / 0.94) 0%, rgb(20 42 36 / 0.86) 55%, rgb(20 42 36 / 0.35) 100%);
    }
  }

  .ab-hero__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.375rem;
  }

  .ab-hero__title {
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 2rem + 3.4vw, 4.25rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 112;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .ab-hero__lede {
    max-width: 30em;
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1rem + 0.4vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .ab-hero__cap {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* The longer version: story on the left, graduation prints on the right. */
  .ab-long {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding-block: 4.5rem 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .ab-long {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
      gap: 3.5rem;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .ab-grad {
      padding-top: 4rem;
    }
  }

  .ab-long__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.125rem;
  }

  .ab-long__text p {
    max-width: 38em;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* The RAMpage paragraph with its build-night print beside it; under it on a phone. */
  .ab-long__rp {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .ab-long__rp :global(.ab-long__print) {
    width: min(55%, 13rem);
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .ab-long__rp {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 11rem;
      gap: 1.75rem;
    }

    .ab-long__rp :global(.ab-long__print) {
      width: 100%;
      margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    }
  }

  .ab-grad {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ab-grad :global(.ab-grad__lead) {
    max-width: 15rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem 0.5rem;
  }

  .ab-grad__pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.5rem;
  }

  .ab-grad__cap {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* Why underwater: the deep band. */
  .ab-why {
    margin-top: 4.5rem;
    background: var(--g-band);
  }

  /* Straight on from the recommendations band, with no strip of page between the two. */
  :global(.pq) + .ab-why {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .ab-why__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .ab-why__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
      gap: 3.5rem;
    }
  }

  .ab-why__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .ab-why__text > p:not(.ab-why__kicker) {
    max-width: 34em;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .ab-why__kicker {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--g-accent);
  }

  /* The prints, each the photo's own shape, two by two; an odd last one sits centered under them. */
  .ab-why__prints {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 32rem;
    padding: 0.5rem;
  }

  .ab-why__prints > :global(:last-child:nth-child(odd)) {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    justify-self: center;
    width: calc(50% - 0.75rem);
  }

  /* Closing band. */
  .ab-end__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: 3.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .ab-end__line {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
